    "more": "Colonization and occupation are systems, held in place by laws, armies and policies, and they can be challenged and ended. Most people living inside a system did not write it, and some were born there and have no other home. That does not excuse the system, and it does not ask the people it harmed to stay quiet. International humanitarian law protects civilians on every side, and treats attacks on them as crimes. Naming the system and refusing the dehumanizing label go together: the first is accurate and the second leaves people unable to imagine an ending that is not more violence. The same care applies the other way, when anyone calls the colonized or the occupied vermin or less than human.",
